WEBVTT

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.761
Senri, why...?

00:00:52.761 --> 00:00:56.348
Do you think I don't know?

00:00:56.348 --> 00:00:59.893
Senri, you don't know anything!

00:01:19.663 --> 00:01:22.416
<i>Writing down my aspirations</i>

00:01:22.416 --> 00:01:25.169
<i>For the day when they will come true</i>

00:01:25.169 --> 00:01:30.507
<i>The time has come when</i>
<i>I want to turn to the page I marked</i>

00:01:30.507 --> 00:01:35.971
<i>Although there are things I lose</i>
<i>sight of with everything that happens</i>

00:01:35.971 --> 00:01:37.347
<i>Hey, it's all right</i>

00:01:37.347 --> 00:01:41.268
<i>The start I'm embarking on is unexpected</i>

00:01:41.268 --> 00:01:44.104
<i>The memory that you couldn't erase</i>

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:46.773
<i>Even that sad memory</i>

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:50.819
<i>I'll give it a different, happier reading</i>

00:01:50.819 --> 00:01:56.450
<i>I feel like just that will change everything</i>

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:57.576
<i>All Right</i>

00:01:57.576 --> 00:02:00.787
<i>So come now, the way you are!</i>

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:03.624
<i>Don't hide your weak self</i>

00:02:03.624 --> 00:02:04.625
<i>On my Sheep </i>

00:02:04.625 --> 00:02:08.295
<i>Let's meet riding on a dream</i>

00:02:08.295 --> 00:02:14.218
<i>Even just calling your name as</i>
<i>I write in this book of adventures</i>

00:02:14.218 --> 00:02:17.054
<i>I'm not lost anymore</i>

00:02:17.054 --> 00:02:20.766
<i>Let's start our journey together</i>

00:02:20.766 --> 00:02:28.524
<i>Yes... more of you and me!</i>

00:02:39.409 --> 00:02:43.914
"Episode 2: Lost and Found"

00:02:49.086 --> 00:02:51.588
Kakei isn't here yet...

00:02:54.466 --> 00:02:58.303
I'm glad I plucked up the courage to ask him.

00:02:59.346 --> 00:03:04.017
Now I just have to work hard
to make sure he isn't disappointed!

00:03:10.649 --> 00:03:12.484
Hello, Kakei.

00:03:12.484 --> 00:03:15.654
Oh, sorry. Is it locked?

00:03:15.654 --> 00:03:18.574
It's okay. I just got here.

00:03:20.784 --> 00:03:21.869
"Storeroom 11-3 (History Books)"
"Library Club"

00:03:21.869 --> 00:03:24.371
This room is mine.

00:03:24.371 --> 00:03:28.125
I can't hand over my quiet place so easily.

00:03:37.509 --> 00:03:38.844
Hey.

00:03:39.636 --> 00:03:40.470
Hey...

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:42.431
Does Master Giza have an owner?

00:03:42.431 --> 00:03:43.473
Dunno.

00:03:43.473 --> 00:03:45.934
I wonder how old he is.

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:47.311
Dunno.

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:54.109
I wonder where he gets his food.

00:03:54.109 --> 00:03:55.527
Dunno.

00:03:55.527 --> 00:03:59.489
Kakei, you really like books, don't you?

00:03:59.489 --> 00:04:02.117
The more you read, the more you know.

00:04:02.117 --> 00:04:04.536
So you like learning, huh?

00:04:04.536 --> 00:04:05.579
Yeah...

00:04:06.622 --> 00:04:09.082
Light to disperse the darkness...

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:12.169
The more I read,
the brighter the world becomes,

00:04:12.169 --> 00:04:14.046
and the closer I get to a peaceful life.

00:04:18.509 --> 00:04:19.676
Open wide!

00:04:20.761 --> 00:04:22.054
Can you tell what flavor this is?

00:04:22.054 --> 00:04:23.055
Lemon.

00:04:24.473 --> 00:04:25.432
Strawberry?

00:04:25.432 --> 00:04:29.561
That's right! You finally looked at me.

00:04:30.604 --> 00:04:32.523
Sorry.

00:04:33.774 --> 00:04:38.403
Kakei, you said you'd hang out
with me until Golden Week, right?

00:04:38.403 --> 00:04:40.322
Huh? Yeah...

00:04:40.322 --> 00:04:44.576
Then I'm going to work hard to make
you want to work together after that, too.

00:04:44.576 --> 00:04:46.620
So, Kakei!

00:04:48.205 --> 00:04:51.416
Won't you... pick up some trash with me?

00:04:53.293 --> 00:04:54.378
Huh?

00:04:56.713 --> 00:05:00.676
Picking up trash can actually
be pretty fun if you do it seriously...

00:05:01.969 --> 00:05:04.763
I think it's called an
odd-jobs club at school...?

00:05:04.763 --> 00:05:06.306
I want this to be a project where

00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:09.852
--we help solve people's problems and worries.
--Please take one!

00:05:11.937 --> 00:05:17.109
But if we suddenly tell people,
"Please ask us for help," no one will trust us.

00:05:17.109 --> 00:05:19.570
So we need to make our name known first,

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:23.699
but we also need to have a
good track record with our activities.

00:05:23.699 --> 00:05:24.950
But...

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:26.952
Isn't picking up trash kind of sad?

00:05:26.952 --> 00:05:29.246
I guess it's no good, huh?

00:05:29.246 --> 00:05:34.918
Well, Shirasaki's the leader,
so let's try what she's thinking first.

00:05:34.918 --> 00:05:36.086
Thanks!

00:05:36.086 --> 00:05:37.713
Oh?

00:05:37.713 --> 00:05:39.673
Hey, Kakei!

00:05:39.673 --> 00:05:41.300
Pass! Here I go!

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:42.426
'Kay!

00:05:43.552 --> 00:05:44.761
One more!

00:05:45.262 --> 00:05:46.513
All right!

00:05:47.055 --> 00:05:48.432
Nice catch!

00:05:48.432 --> 00:05:49.474
Not yet.

00:05:49.474 --> 00:05:52.352
Hey, stop playing around!

00:05:57.274 --> 00:05:58.525
Sorry.

00:05:58.525 --> 00:06:00.110
Hey!

00:06:02.154 --> 00:06:04.114
I said sorry!

00:06:08.035 --> 00:06:13.248
We're the Shiomi Happy Project.
Won't you pick up trash with us?

00:06:13.248 --> 00:06:15.334
We have cotton gloves and tongs for you to use,

00:06:15.334 --> 00:06:19.880
and you can leave whenever you want.

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:23.258
Picking up trash isn't something
that'll catch on anytime soon, huh?

00:06:23.258 --> 00:06:26.845
Well, if we keep doing it, someone will come.

00:06:27.846 --> 00:06:29.640
It's like picking up girls, huh?

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:31.433
Have you done that before, Kakei?

00:06:31.433 --> 00:06:32.684
No, never.

00:06:32.684 --> 00:06:36.563
That's too bad.
I'm sure you'd get a lot of girls.

00:06:38.065 --> 00:06:40.484
Would I be able to get you, Shirasaki?

00:06:40.484 --> 00:06:44.863
Huh? I-I don't know...

00:06:44.863 --> 00:06:46.490
I was just kidding.

00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:49.409
--Don't turn red from that.
--What? Huh?

00:06:54.122 --> 00:06:55.999
We're the Shiomi Happy Project.

00:06:57.334 --> 00:07:00.796
Uh, um... Kakei...?

00:07:00.796 --> 00:07:04.174
Oh, are you from Appllio?

00:07:04.174 --> 00:07:07.052
Yes, I am! I'm Suzuki.

00:07:07.052 --> 00:07:09.429
I'm so happy you remembered me.

00:07:09.429 --> 00:07:11.765
Did I tell you my name?

00:07:11.765 --> 00:07:14.226
It was on the web news--

00:07:14.226 --> 00:07:16.270
Even though it looked like
you were a molester at first,

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:19.940
you were actually a hero
that saved a female student.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:24.653
"Shiomi Academy Journalism Club News"

00:07:24.653 --> 00:07:25.362
"Shiomi Academy Journalism Club News"
Mochizuki must have kept her promise.

00:07:25.362 --> 00:07:27.364
"[Important] Apology and Correction"
Mochizuki must have kept her promise.

00:07:27.364 --> 00:07:29.867
"Regarding Article from the Derailing Accident"
I guess I owe her one now.

00:07:30.826 --> 00:07:33.495
You look like you're
doing something interesting.

00:07:33.495 --> 00:07:35.539
Oh, if you're interested, do you want to join--?

00:07:35.539 --> 00:07:37.207
Yeah, sure!

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:40.294
Thank you, thank you!

00:07:40.294 --> 00:07:42.296
Are you all right? I hope
you don't feel forced into it.

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:45.924
I love this kind of thing.

00:07:45.924 --> 00:07:48.802
I'm Kana Suzuki. I'll work hard!

00:08:02.149 --> 00:08:04.026
Looking for something?

00:08:04.026 --> 00:08:05.986
Are you all right? Need help?

00:08:05.986 --> 00:08:07.821
Um, no...

00:08:07.821 --> 00:08:10.157
Thank you for the offer.

00:08:10.157 --> 00:08:12.326
Your clothes will get dirty, too.

00:08:12.326 --> 00:08:15.454
"Senri Misono"

00:08:16.705 --> 00:08:17.706
That, huh?

00:08:17.706 --> 00:08:20.167
Um, it's really quite all right.

00:08:20.167 --> 00:08:23.128
All right, just a little...

00:08:24.922 --> 00:08:27.883
Okay... Got it...

00:08:30.636 --> 00:08:31.428
Here.

00:08:31.428 --> 00:08:33.805
Th-Thank you very much.

00:08:33.805 --> 00:08:37.017
500 yen, huh? That's worth trying to get.

00:08:37.017 --> 00:08:39.186
Yes, it's a lot of money.

00:08:42.731 --> 00:08:46.443
I'm sorry, you ended up getting dirty.

00:08:46.443 --> 00:08:48.695
It's all right, I was picking up trash anyway.

00:08:48.695 --> 00:08:49.488
Later.

00:08:49.488 --> 00:08:50.864
Um, please wait.

00:08:53.867 --> 00:08:57.037
This is for you. Thank you.

00:08:59.414 --> 00:09:01.333
No, thank you.

00:09:01.333 --> 00:09:03.627
Please excuse me.

00:09:17.015 --> 00:09:18.016
"Shiomi Academy
⬅ Garbage Collection Area  ⬆ Laboratory Building"

00:09:18.016 --> 00:09:21.353
Man, I worked hard. Really hard.

00:09:22.563 --> 00:09:24.606
We picked up a lot, huh?

00:09:25.399 --> 00:09:28.527
Yay, let's commemorate our first activity!

00:09:30.612 --> 00:09:34.908
Regarding the Shepherd we
were talking about yesterday...

00:09:34.908 --> 00:09:38.954
I compiled the information
I found online here.

00:09:40.622 --> 00:09:44.626
You found all this in one night? That's amazing.

00:09:44.626 --> 00:09:46.712
I just copy-and-pasted the articles I found.

00:09:46.712 --> 00:09:49.089
Anyone could do this.

00:09:49.089 --> 00:09:51.300
Thanks, Tamamo!

00:09:52.509 --> 00:09:55.429
Most are just rumors
that look like urban legends.

00:09:56.513 --> 00:09:59.349
There are even variations
on how the Shepherd manifests.

00:09:59.349 --> 00:10:02.060
Sometimes it's through letters,
sometimes they talk in person.

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:05.022
When the person does what the
Shepherd says, their wishes come true.

00:10:05.772 --> 00:10:07.316
That's the gist of it.

00:10:07.316 --> 00:10:09.526
There aren't any that were through email...

00:10:10.527 --> 00:10:13.113
Speaking of which,
I tried responding to that email,

00:10:13.113 --> 00:10:14.823
but I haven't gotten a reply yet.

00:10:14.823 --> 00:10:16.283
You replied?!

00:10:16.283 --> 00:10:18.076
What if it's spam?

00:10:18.076 --> 00:10:20.662
Well, it's not like it'd kill me.

00:10:21.997 --> 00:10:26.919
Actually, I got an email
from the Shepherd yesterday.

00:10:26.919 --> 00:10:29.630
Something about a fateful encounter...

00:10:30.214 --> 00:10:31.256
Wh-What is it?

00:10:31.256 --> 00:10:34.885
Kana, this is fate!

00:10:37.721 --> 00:10:41.350
Then all of you got emails
from the Shepherd, too...?

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:43.810
Will you show us the email you received?

00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:47.147
Sorry, it's on my computer...

00:10:47.147 --> 00:10:49.775
I don't have a cell phone right now...

00:10:49.775 --> 00:10:51.235
You don't have a cell phone?

00:10:51.235 --> 00:10:54.571
No, I broke it...

00:10:56.823 --> 00:11:00.160
--Kana, your hair is really pretty!
--I'm hungry! Wanna grab something to eat?

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:01.662
--Yeah, it's true!
--I'm hungry! Wanna grab something to eat?

00:11:01.662 --> 00:11:03.413
Yeah, sounds good.

00:11:12.589 --> 00:11:15.050
A tuning fork...?

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:16.552
From the music department?

00:11:18.387 --> 00:11:20.764
No, there's something written on it.

00:11:20.764 --> 00:11:23.851
"Winner" "3rd Junior Vocal Music Competition"
It probably belongs to someone.

00:11:25.561 --> 00:11:30.941
That makes five, and the key
to the sixth person is set, too.

00:11:30.941 --> 00:11:35.028
Get along now, everyone.

00:11:40.826 --> 00:11:45.789
How did you like Miyu Serizawa's
After School Avenue?

00:11:45.789 --> 00:11:51.128
We have Senri Misono's
angelic voice to end us for today.

00:11:51.128 --> 00:11:52.296
Until tomorrow.

00:11:52.296 --> 00:11:54.298
"Entrance Ceremony"

00:12:02.306 --> 00:12:08.437
I'm sorry, we decided to stop
doing the lost and found segment

00:12:08.437 --> 00:12:10.647
because we got too many...

00:12:12.649 --> 00:12:14.359
Where...

00:12:14.359 --> 00:12:16.195
...did you find that?

00:12:16.195 --> 00:12:17.529
On Main Street...

00:12:17.529 --> 00:12:19.239
May I see it...?

00:12:19.239 --> 00:12:23.160
Sure, do you happen to know who it belongs to?

00:12:24.369 --> 00:12:28.457
Do I ever... It belongs to Senri Misono.

00:12:28.457 --> 00:12:29.583
Misono?

00:12:29.583 --> 00:12:30.792
The Song Princess?

00:12:30.792 --> 00:12:32.836
Isn't she super famous?

00:12:34.087 --> 00:12:34.922
Who?

00:12:34.922 --> 00:12:36.507
Kakei, you don't know her?

00:12:36.507 --> 00:12:39.092
I'm sorry, all this kid does is read,

00:12:39.092 --> 00:12:40.719
so he doesn't know anything of the world.

00:12:41.762 --> 00:12:44.806
She's a promising new student
in this year's music department.

00:12:44.806 --> 00:12:49.394
She even sang a special program
at this year's entrance ceremony.

00:12:49.394 --> 00:12:50.646
Really?

00:12:50.646 --> 00:12:55.859
Yes, it was amazing,
like the actual voice of an angel.

00:12:58.237 --> 00:13:02.866
I see, she's kept this all these years...

00:13:05.786 --> 00:13:08.038
It sounded like there was
more than she was telling us.

00:13:08.038 --> 00:13:08.914
Yeah...

00:13:08.914 --> 00:13:13.377
It's already late, so we should
contact Misono tomorrow.

00:13:13.377 --> 00:13:15.671
Suzuki, sorry for making you come with us.

00:13:16.672 --> 00:13:18.924
No problem!

00:13:18.924 --> 00:13:21.718
Can I join you tomorrow, too?

00:13:21.718 --> 00:13:23.220
Yes, of course.

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:25.806
We'll be waiting at our
clubroom in the main library!

00:13:25.806 --> 00:13:28.267
Okay! See you tomorrow, then!

00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:37.568
I'm going to go, after all.

00:13:37.568 --> 00:13:38.652
Go where?

00:13:38.652 --> 00:13:41.613
To Misono's house. You guys go home first.

00:13:41.613 --> 00:13:43.365
See you tomorrow!

00:13:43.365 --> 00:13:44.700
Shirasaki!

00:13:47.786 --> 00:13:48.620
Wait, I'll go, too--

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:52.833
Oh, wait, wait. Leave this to Kakei.

00:13:52.833 --> 00:13:56.753
He almost never volunteers
to do anything on his own.

00:13:59.173 --> 00:14:01.425
Sorry to make you come, too, Kakei.

00:14:01.425 --> 00:14:03.927
I'd be worried about
you going alone, Shirasaki.

00:14:03.927 --> 00:14:07.097
Oh, you don't trust me.

00:14:09.975 --> 00:14:15.731
I know that I don't have to go today...

00:14:15.731 --> 00:14:17.566
But...

00:14:17.566 --> 00:14:22.029
I think this probably means a lot to her.

00:14:22.029 --> 00:14:26.116
Misono might be sad that she lost it,

00:14:26.116 --> 00:14:29.453
and I don't want her to feel that way.

00:14:29.453 --> 00:14:31.455
Even though you've never met her?

00:14:32.915 --> 00:14:34.249
Yeah.

00:14:35.709 --> 00:14:37.586
Hey, Shirasaki...

00:14:37.586 --> 00:14:39.713
Why are you trying so hard?

00:14:39.713 --> 00:14:40.589
Huh?

00:14:40.589 --> 00:14:42.883
You said you wanted to change yourself, right?

00:14:42.883 --> 00:14:45.135
Why did you start something like this?

00:14:45.135 --> 00:14:46.595
It's because...

00:14:53.894 --> 00:14:55.354
Misono?

00:14:58.023 --> 00:15:01.860
The upperclassman from the vending machine?

00:15:03.946 --> 00:15:06.657
We found this on Main Street and picked it up.

00:15:06.657 --> 00:15:09.159
We heard it was yours...

00:15:09.159 --> 00:15:11.078
Thank you very much!

00:15:11.078 --> 00:15:13.914
I couldn't find it anywhere,
and I thought I'd never see it again!

00:15:13.914 --> 00:15:15.999
You were looking for it after all, huh?

00:15:15.999 --> 00:15:20.879
Yes. I went to the vending machine from lunch

00:15:20.879 --> 00:15:22.589
but couldn't find it there, either.

00:15:22.589 --> 00:15:24.174
Is it something important?

00:15:25.592 --> 00:15:27.845
It is full of memories.

00:15:27.845 --> 00:15:29.721
Precious memories...

00:15:31.849 --> 00:15:34.518
Really, thank you very much.

00:15:34.518 --> 00:15:36.728
You helped me again, huh?

00:15:36.728 --> 00:15:40.023
It's the first time I ever
saw such a pretty tuning fork.

00:15:40.023 --> 00:15:42.401
As expected of the Song Princess--

00:15:44.319 --> 00:15:48.991
Did you bring it to me
because I'm the Song Princess?

00:15:48.991 --> 00:15:50.784
Huh?

00:15:53.328 --> 00:15:56.874
No, it's because you
showed us something good.

00:16:02.045 --> 00:16:04.006
Something good?

00:16:04.006 --> 00:16:08.093
Seriously speaking, we're doing
kind of a volunteer service right now.

00:16:08.093 --> 00:16:09.511
Right, Shirasaki?

00:16:09.511 --> 00:16:12.097
Oh, yeah...

00:16:12.431 --> 00:16:13.765
Here.

00:16:15.309 --> 00:16:17.978
"Shiomi Happy Project"...?

00:16:17.978 --> 00:16:21.773
If you ever need help,
don't hesitate to contact us.

00:16:30.741 --> 00:16:34.286
I never want to feel that way again...

00:16:37.956 --> 00:16:40.125
I'll come back later, after all.

00:16:40.125 --> 00:16:41.335
Suzuki?

00:16:42.628 --> 00:16:46.173
G-Good evening. Are you on your way home?

00:16:46.173 --> 00:16:47.508
Yeah.

00:16:47.508 --> 00:16:49.218
Suzuki, you're buying a cell phone?

00:16:49.218 --> 00:16:52.763
Um, yes, that's right.

00:16:53.722 --> 00:16:57.059
Kakei, will you look at them with me?

00:16:57.059 --> 00:16:58.435
Sure, I guess.

00:16:58.435 --> 00:17:01.104
Really? Thank you!

00:17:01.104 --> 00:17:02.314
What happened after that?

00:17:04.358 --> 00:17:06.527
--Oh, that's cute.
--What the heck?

00:17:06.985 --> 00:17:08.487
It looks hard to use.

00:17:08.487 --> 00:17:11.198
Oh, but it's so cute. Look.

00:17:11.198 --> 00:17:13.742
It's like, hop, hop!

00:17:13.742 --> 00:17:15.994
Simple is best, in my opinion.

00:17:15.994 --> 00:17:18.038
Oh, that's smart looking.

00:17:18.038 --> 00:17:20.499
As expected of a <i>smart </i>phone.

00:17:20.499 --> 00:17:21.625
Right?

00:17:21.625 --> 00:17:25.087
Then, what if I got a matching phone?

00:17:25.087 --> 00:17:26.463
Please don't.

00:17:26.463 --> 00:17:30.133
Hey Kakei, that hurt my feelings.

00:17:30.133 --> 00:17:34.680
It's something you'll be using every day,
so you should get something you like.

00:17:35.764 --> 00:17:36.807
Okay.

00:17:46.233 --> 00:17:48.652
Hello, Kakei.

00:17:48.652 --> 00:17:50.404
Sorry, were you waiting long?

00:17:50.404 --> 00:17:52.990
No, I just got here.

00:17:54.491 --> 00:17:56.285
Good work yesterday.

00:17:56.994 --> 00:18:00.163
I'm glad Misono's Happy Project worked out.

00:18:00.163 --> 00:18:01.081
Huh?

00:18:01.081 --> 00:18:04.459
Oh no, that was something that looked important,

00:18:04.459 --> 00:18:06.920
so I just wanted to get it
to her as soon as possible.

00:18:08.297 --> 00:18:09.965
I have to work hard today, too.

00:18:09.965 --> 00:18:13.010
Let's make the school more and more "Happy"!

00:18:14.344 --> 00:18:19.349
Could it be that unlike me, she's really...

00:18:20.058 --> 00:18:21.351
Kakei?

00:18:22.895 --> 00:18:26.231
Here's the key to this room.
You should take care of it.

00:18:29.067 --> 00:18:30.152
Is that all right?

00:18:30.152 --> 00:18:32.154
I did decide to work with you.

00:18:33.155 --> 00:18:35.991
Thanks, I'll take good care of it.

00:18:35.991 --> 00:18:37.784
It's just the key to the clubroom.

00:18:37.784 --> 00:18:39.703
Can I put a keychain on it?

00:18:39.703 --> 00:18:41.246
Do whatever you want.

00:18:41.246 --> 00:18:43.540
You can make spare keys for everyone, too.

00:18:43.540 --> 00:18:44.416
Just don't lose it, okay?

00:18:44.416 --> 00:18:46.293
I-I won't lose it!

00:18:48.045 --> 00:18:51.590
This is Miyu Serizawa's After School Avenue.

00:18:51.590 --> 00:18:56.929
For the next thirty minutes,
take a walk with me.

00:18:56.929 --> 00:18:59.431
She sounds really different from yesterday.

00:18:59.431 --> 00:19:01.350
As expected of a pro.

00:19:06.605 --> 00:19:09.608
Ta-da! A new cell phone!

00:19:09.608 --> 00:19:10.317
Ooh--

00:19:10.317 --> 00:19:11.610
Oh, it's cute!

00:19:11.610 --> 00:19:13.529
An SM-04D?

00:19:13.529 --> 00:19:15.781
I was looking at this, too!

00:19:15.781 --> 00:19:17.991
Let's trade email addresses!

00:19:17.991 --> 00:19:21.787
No fair, Takamine.
I want Kana's email address, too!

00:19:21.787 --> 00:19:24.873
Calm down, you guys. You're scaring Suzuki.

00:19:28.877 --> 00:19:31.338
Thank you, everyone.

00:19:31.338 --> 00:19:32.965
Huh? Why?

00:19:35.801 --> 00:19:37.344
You're too loud!

00:19:37.344 --> 00:19:38.720
Oh, sorry.

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:39.972
You're too loud.

00:19:39.972 --> 00:19:41.056
Now, now.

00:19:41.056 --> 00:19:42.474
You're too loud.

00:19:42.474 --> 00:19:44.935
You don't have to keep saying it.
We can hear you.

00:19:44.935 --> 00:19:47.187
Then why don't you look more apologetic?!

00:19:47.187 --> 00:19:49.273
Your squeals and shouts
can be heard through the door...

00:19:49.273 --> 00:19:51.650
Wait, did you get another one?

00:19:51.650 --> 00:19:54.820
Hello, I'm Kana Suzuki, a new member.

00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:58.240
Kana, you'll join the club?

00:19:58.240 --> 00:19:59.700
I said, stop yelling!

00:19:59.700 --> 00:20:02.661
Now, now. Why don't you
look at the cat and calm down?

00:20:06.331 --> 00:20:08.625
Come on, hold me tight.

00:20:12.004 --> 00:20:12.796
What's wrong?

00:20:12.796 --> 00:20:14.715
D-Do something...

00:20:14.715 --> 00:20:16.717
Oh, you don't like cats?

00:20:16.717 --> 00:20:20.554
I-I don't like a-animals...

00:20:20.554 --> 00:20:22.764
Sorry, I didn't realize.

00:20:24.141 --> 00:20:28.020
A-Anyway, just be quiet, okay?

00:20:39.239 --> 00:20:41.825
Is this really all right with you, Suzuki?

00:20:41.825 --> 00:20:43.577
You don't have to be so formal.

00:20:43.577 --> 00:20:46.538
Yesterday, I had more fun
than I'd had in a long time,

00:20:46.538 --> 00:20:49.666
so now I want to hang out with you all more.

00:20:54.546 --> 00:21:01.595
"Senri Misono will teach you
something important. From the Shepherd."

00:21:01.595 --> 00:21:04.139
Wh-What is this?

00:21:04.139 --> 00:21:06.433
Did you give anyone that email address?

00:21:06.433 --> 00:21:08.519
I didn't give it to anyone yet...

00:21:08.519 --> 00:21:10.729
This is not normal, after all.

00:21:10.729 --> 00:21:14.858
Whoever's sending these
is obviously watching us.

00:21:14.858 --> 00:21:17.945
Does this person want us to contact Misono?

00:21:17.945 --> 00:21:22.491
Maybe someone good with
computers can tell who's sending these?

00:21:22.491 --> 00:21:24.910
Depends on how good they are.

00:21:24.910 --> 00:21:28.497
There <i>is </i>someone--the genius
who's the pride of the school cafeteria...

00:21:29.039 --> 00:21:31.124
Chicken breast cooked in rice malt

00:21:31.124 --> 00:21:33.627
"Student Cafeteria - Appllio"
and a Caesar salad and panini

00:21:33.627 --> 00:21:35.003
comes to 1000 yen.

00:21:35.003 --> 00:21:36.755
And your smile!

00:21:36.755 --> 00:21:40.217
Okay, that'll be an additional 10,000 yen.

00:21:51.144 --> 00:21:59.903
<i>The starting bell, the sound of a lock</i>

00:21:59.903 --> 00:22:07.578
<i>While drifting aimlessly, I become an adult</i>

00:22:07.578 --> 00:22:17.421
<i>The time has come when days spent</i>
<i>running and playing seem far away</i>

00:22:17.421 --> 00:22:21.675
<i>The answer I gave here</i>

00:22:21.675 --> 00:22:34.605
<i>Oh, if only it had been</i>
<i>passed down somewhere</i>

00:22:34.605 --> 00:22:39.401
<i>For those crowds walking around lost</i>

00:22:39.401 --> 00:22:43.739
<i>It can be a light that shines on them</i>

00:22:43.739 --> 00:22:52.039
<i>On the other side of the</i>
<i>green belt that surrounds us</i>

00:22:52.039 --> 00:23:00.422
<i>You head toward endless tomorrows</i>

00:23:12.809 --> 00:23:15.521
How about this one? But this one's nice, too.

00:23:15.521 --> 00:23:16.813
You look happy, Shirasaki.

00:23:16.813 --> 00:23:20.275
Tamamo! Kakei gave me
the key to the library club!

00:23:20.275 --> 00:23:21.652
Th-That's nice...

00:23:21.652 --> 00:23:24.404
Yeah! Which keychain should I get...?

00:23:24.404 --> 00:23:28.200
Kakei... Are you trying to raise
Shirasaki's happiness levels with the key?

00:23:28.200 --> 00:23:30.452
At this rate, my Shirasaki will be...

00:23:30.452 --> 00:23:31.912
Tamamo, which one do you like?

00:23:31.912 --> 00:23:37.046
"Next time: Lonely Song Princess"
You should decide that, Shirasaki...
